  "explanation": "Likely cause from source inspection: the original rotary kernel distributes its work across 384 CTAs. Fusion uses 16 or 32 attention CTAs, adds serial rotary work, and repeats key rotations for each query tile. Direct global-to-shared rotary staging removes extra shared reads/barriers and reuses rotary factors across Q/K, but still loses. Exact FP32 product/add roundings and BF16 boundaries were retained. Hardware counters were unavailable, so the precise stall attribution is unmeasured.",
